Bare reads of class fields inside methods (diag.unqualified_field_read,
warning): a :RETURN value, an :IF condition, a call argument, a subscript
and a member-access receiver. A name followed by ( is a call and must not
flag.
-- input.ssl --
:CLASS Gate;
:DECLARE bReady, aSlots, nPos, oOwner;

:PROCEDURE Check;
	:IF bReady;
		UsrMes("ready");
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN aSlots[nPos];
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE OwnerName;
	:DECLARE sName;
	sName := oOwner:GetName();
	UsrMes(LimsString(Len(aSlots)));
	:RETURN sName;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:CLASS Gate;
:DECLARE bReady, aSlots, nPos, oOwner;

:PROCEDURE Check;
	:IF bReady;
		UsrMes("ready");
	:ENDIF;

	:RETURN aSlots[nPos];
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE OwnerName;
	:DECLARE sName;

	sName := oOwner:GetName();
	UsrMes(LimsString(Len(aSlots)));

	:RETURN sName;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
5:6-5:12 warning unqualified_field_read: Bare 'bReady' inside a class method does not read the class field — it resolves to a local, a caller's variable, or a public, and raises 'Variable [bReady] is undefined!' when none exists. Use 'Me:bReady'
8:10-8:16 warning unqualified_field_read: Bare 'aSlots' inside a class method does not read the class field — it resolves to a local, a caller's variable, or a public, and raises 'Variable [aSlots] is undefined!' when none exists. Use 'Me:aSlots'
8:17-8:21 warning unqualified_field_read: Bare 'nPos' inside a class method does not read the class field — it resolves to a local, a caller's variable, or a public, and raises 'Variable [nPos] is undefined!' when none exists. Use 'Me:nPos'
13:11-13:17 warning unqualified_field_read: Bare 'oOwner' inside a class method does not read the class field — it resolves to a local, a caller's variable, or a public, and raises 'Variable [oOwner] is undefined!' when none exists. Use 'Me:oOwner'
14:24-14:30 warning unqualified_field_read: Bare 'aSlots' inside a class method does not read the class field — it resolves to a local, a caller's variable, or a public, and raises 'Variable [aSlots] is undefined!' when none exists. Use 'Me:aSlots'
